From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zed-patches <zed-patches@localhost>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:31:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: send a sub-thread's result to its parent, and list
 sub-threads as task items

Story 039 opens a sub-thread from a selected excerpt of an agent message and
records its parent in 0048's organization store. Nothing carried the outcome
back, and nothing showed which sub-threads exist or which one is still working.
This patch adds both halves (story 040).

Send to Parent. A sub-thread's composer footer gets a "Send to Parent" menu
with two choices, each a Tab stop with a tooltip and an accessible label:
  - "Send Last Reply" puts the last agent reply, under a header naming the
    sub-thread (`From sub-thread "<title>":`), into the parent's composer;
  - "Summarize and Send" asks the sub-thread for a summary in a visible turn
    and delivers that turn's reply the same way, only when the turn the
    request itself started ends with end of turn.
The text is appended after any draft and never sent: the operator reviews it.
A closed parent is opened first through 0040's router; a reply over 200,000
characters is cut on a char boundary with a count of what was left out. Both
choices are disabled, with the reason as tooltip, when the parent was deleted,
while a delivery is still reaching the parent, while a turn runs or a summary
waits, and (Summarize only) while a reported-activity session has not reported
since it loaded. The summary is bound to its own SUMMARY_REQUEST entry, not to
the activity generation alone: on the reported-activity transport the agent can
start a turn of its own that takes the generation the summary expected. A
request the agent rejects on that transport settles its submission Failed
with no turn and no Error event; that clears the summary too, the error shown
under the control.

Sub-thread items. A reporter in agent_ui turns 039's links and the sub-thread
threads' run state into SubThreadActivity (Linked, Running, Idle, Retitled),
emitted by 0037's tasks card beside its TaskActivity and replayed when a store
registers. 0035's TaskHistoryStore records each as an item under the parent's
session, task id `zeo-sub-thread:<sub session>`, kind `sub_thread`, so it
groups, archives and deletes through the same TaskKey paths as the adapter's
tasks. The card and the panel draw it with a "Sub-thread" chip, Running or
Idle, no Stop, no log; activating it opens the sub-thread, or says the thread
no longer exists.

History schema. Two steps appended to AgentTaskHistoryDb's migrations, steps
1-4 untouched:
  - step 5: `origin TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT "adapter"` -- the stored column alone
    says what an item is; every sub-thread write is guarded on it, so a row the
    adapter wrote on the same key is never rewritten, and an unknown origin a
    newer Zeo wrote is skipped with a warning, like an unknown status;
  - step 6: `deleted INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` -- deleting an archived
    sub-thread item keeps a hidden tombstone, because the parent link outlives
    the delete and the next start would record the item again. load_all skips
    it, deleted_sub_thread_keys() seeds the store's deleted set before the
    replay, and neither sub-thread write revives it. Adapter rows are still
    removed as before.
0056's log_bytes test pinned its step as the last migration; it now pins it by
its index (3), since step 5 follows it; the length is still never pinned.

Touch points in upstream and earlier-patch files: ThreadView gains the state
field, its focus handle and one footer call, and get_agent_message_content
becomes pub(crate); ConversationView::handle_thread_event forwards Stopped,
Error, Refusal, EntriesRemoved and SubmissionUpdated to the sub-thread view; tasks_card.rs and
agent_tasks_panel's panel.rs dispatch on the origin; agent_ui.rs re-exports
the reporter's types. Logs carry session ids, statuses and counts only, never a
title or a reply (zeo_sub_thread event=...).

Last of the claude-agent-acp-plus group, after 0070 whose sub-threads it
consumes. 115 tests added (unit, GPUI integration and history migrations).

Story 064 (2026-11-02): Zeo's task surfaces read Zed's native subagent
registry, beside the adapter's feed.
  - One row per child. tasks_card::merge folds a feed task into the
    registry's row only when their child session ids are equal, never on a
    title; the registry's status wins (Waiting and Unknown included), the
    feed's usage, last tool and summary are carried. TaskRow gains `source`
    (ClaudeTasks | AcpSubagent { child, can_cancel }) and its own
    TaskRowStatus.
  - The card. A row appears on SubagentSpawned alone; Stop sends
    session/cancel to that child when it allows it and is disabled with the
    reason otherwise, a cancel error shown on the row; Open shows the child.
  - The panel. Live rows under their parent; Open on a child the parent does
    not hold opens the parent at its card with a notice (0041's
    open_agent_subagent); agent_panel handles the card's OpenNativeSubagent.
  - History step 7: `child_session_id TEXT`, appended, steps 1-6 untouched;
    TaskOrigin gains acp_subagent and a record's id is
    `acp-subagent:<child>`, though the id prefix never decides the origin.
    A 0.7.0 database (test_data/history_0_7_0.sql, and the operator's real db
    copied to scratch) reads back byte for byte with a NULL child.
  - Restored outcomes are not endings: a child whose first observed status is
    terminal is shown Done and recorded nowhere.
  - Waiting reads Waiting. A child in RequiresAction reads "Waiting for you"
    on the card's progress line and in the panel's status text, in the
    warning colour, where both used to say Running: the card reads the row's
    TaskRowStatus, and the panel a live-only `waiting` field on TaskRecord
    that panel_row lays over the stored record (TasksCard::live_task_waiting).
    AgentTaskStatus still folds Waiting into Running, so expiry, the history
    and the tray are unchanged, and the field is never stored.
It lands here because 0071 is the last patch of the group that touches
tasks_card.rs, the history and the panel. 46 tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
